<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
<section id="S1a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">A </span>Pilot Experiment Details</h2>

<div id="S1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the detailed settings for the pilot experiment in Figure <a href="#S1.F2" title="Figure 2 ‣ 1 Introduction ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S1.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.1 </span>Datasets</h3>

<div id="S1.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To test the gradient entanglement between preferred and dispreferred trajectories, we plot their angles and norms for three different datasets. The difference in trajectory length between the three datasets is illustrated in Figure <a href="#S1.F9" title="Figure 9 ‣ A.1 Datasets ‣ A Pilot Experiment Details ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">9</span></a>.</p>
<ul id="S1.I1" class="ltx_itemize">
<li id="S1.I1.i1" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Stanford IMDb</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib21" title="" class="ltx_ref">Maas et al., 2011</a>)</cite>: A movie classification dataset with single-token (Positive/Negative) preferred and dispreferred trajectories.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i2" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Anthropic Helpful and Harmless</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib1" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bai et al., 2022</a>)</cite>: A commonly used RLHF dataset with moderately long preferred and dispreferred trajectories.</p>
</div></li>
<li id="S1.I1.i3" class="ltx_item" style="list-style-type:none;"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_item">•</span> 
<div id="S1.I1.i3.p1" class="ltx_para">
<p id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S1.I1.i3.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Hendrycks MATH dataset</span> <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib10" title="" class="ltx_ref">Hendrycks et al., 2021</a>)</cite>: A commonly used math dataset with long, gradient entangled preferred and dispreferred trajectories.</p>
</div></li>
</ul>
</div>
<figure id="S1.F9" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19893v1/figure9.svg" id="S1.F9.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:329/195;" width="329" height="195"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 9: </span>Token lengths for each dataset. IMDb consists of 1 token long trajectories, HH with moderately long trajectories, while MATH consists of long trajectories.</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S1.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">A.2 </span>Training Settings</h3>

<div id="S1.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S1.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We fine-tune the Qwen2.5-1.5B model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib27" title="" class="ltx_ref">Qwen et al., 2024</a>)</cite> on the IMDb, HH, and MATH datasets using the SimPER algorithm <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib33" title="" class="ltx_ref">Xiao et al., 2025</a>)</cite>. For the MATH dataset, we use the same preference data as described below for the Qwen2.5-Math-7B model. For IMDb and HH, we use the originally provided datasets. We conduct all training under a single NVIDIA A100 GPU with 80GB of RAM. We use a cosine learning rate scheduler. Table <a href="#S1.T4" title="Table 4 ‣ A.2 Training Settings ‣ A Pilot Experiment Details ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a> shows the detailed hyperparameters.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S1.T4" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 4: </span>Pilot experiment hyperparameters.</figcaption>
<table id="S1.T4.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S1.T4.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S1.T4.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Parameter</span></th>
<th id="S1.T4.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S1.T4.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Value</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S1.T4.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Seed</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_t">42</td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.3" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.3.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Optimizer</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.3.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">AdamW (<math id="S1.T4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta_{1}=0.9,\beta_{2}=0.999" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>1</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.9</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>β</mi><mn>2</mn></msub><mo>=</mo><mn>0.999</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta_{1}=0.9,\beta_{2}=0.999</annotation></semantics></math>)</td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.4" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.4.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Warmup Steps</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.4.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">150</td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.5" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.5.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Learning Rate</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.5.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><math id="S1.T4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 10^{-6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn>5</mn><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mn>10</mn><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>6</mn></mrow></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 10^{-6}</annotation></semantics></math></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.6" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.6.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Max Gradient Norm</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.6.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">10</td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.7" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.7.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Max Steps</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.7.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">25,000</td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.8" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.8.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Batch Size</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.8.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left">64</td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.9" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.9.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row">Precision</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.9.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left"><span id="S1.T4.2.9.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_typewriter">bfloat16</span></td></tr>
<tr id="S1.T4.2.10" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S1.T4.2.10.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_bb">Max Sequence Length</th>
<td id="S1.T4.2.10.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_border_bb">2,048</td></tr>
</tbody>
</table>
</figure>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S2a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">B </span>Theoretical Background</h2>

<div id="S2a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">In this section, we theoretically analyze the robustness of DPO and SimPER when applied to mathematical reasoning tasks.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.1 </span>Limitations of DPO with Deterministic Preferences</h3>

<div id="S2.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Direct Preference Optimization (DPO) may not be robust in mathematical reasoning tasks due to its reliance on the Bradley-Terry model <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib2" title="" class="ltx_ref">Bradley &amp; Terry, 1952</a>)</cite>. Under this model, DPO assumes that preference pairs are selected based on an unknown reward function <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math>, where the probability that response <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> is preferred over <math id="S2.SS1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> follows:</p>
<table id="S2.EGx7" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.E7"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle p^{*}(y_{w}\succ y_{l}\mid x)=\frac{\exp(r^{*}(x,y_{w}))}{\exp(r^{*}(x,y_{w}))+\exp(r^{*}(x,y_{l}))}=\sigma\!\big(r^{*}(x,y_{w})-r^{*}(x,y_{l})\big)." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>+</mo><mrow><mi>exp</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle p^{*}(y_{w}\succ y_{l}\mid x)=\frac{\exp(r^{*}(x,y_{w}))}{\exp(r^{*}(x,y_{w}))+\exp(r^{*}(x,y_{l}))}=\sigma\!\big(r^{*}(x,y_{w})-r^{*}(x,y_{l})\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(7)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">This assumption becomes problematic in mathematical reasoning tasks, where preference pairs consist of clearly correct and incorrect answers, yielding deterministic preferences: <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="p^{*}(y_{w}\succ y_{l}\mid x)=1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>p</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>≻</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub></mrow><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">p^{*}(y_{w}\succ y_{l}\mid x)=1</annotation></semantics></math>. As <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib6" title="" class="ltx_ref">Gheshlaghi Azar et al. (2024)</a></cite> and <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citet"><a href="#bib.bib5" title="" class="ltx_ref">Fisch et al. (2025)</a></cite> show, deterministic preferences require <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="r^{*}(y_{w})-r^{*}(y_{l})\to\infty" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msup><mi>r</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">∞</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">r^{*}(y_{w})-r^{*}(y_{l})\to\infty</annotation></semantics></math> in the Bradley-Terry model, forcing <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta^{*}}(y_{l}\mid x)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><msup><mi>θ</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta^{*}}(y_{l}\mid x)=0</annotation></semantics></math> regardless of the KL regularization strength <math id="S2.SS1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\beta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>β</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\beta</annotation></semantics></math>. Since mathematical reasoning trajectories often share a large number of common tokens between preferred and dispreferred sequences, this over-penalization of the dispreferred sequences can lead to a degradation of the model’s overall performance.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S2.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">B.2 </span>Theoretical Advantages of SimPER</h3>

<div id="S2.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Unlike DPO’s reliance on the Bradley-Terry model, SimPER can be understood as an offline policy gradient method with sequence-length normalization. This formulation aligns naturally with the deterministic reward structure in the mathematical reasoning domain. It makes the learning objective coincide with the data-generating process, thereby eliminating model assumption misspecification.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.p2.1" class="ltx_p">We begin by establishing the notation used throughout our analysis.</p>
</div>
<section id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">Notation.</h4>

<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Let <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math> be the input space and <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> the set of all finite token sequences.
For <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math>, let <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="|y|" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">|y|</annotation></semantics></math> denote its length.
We denote the language model policy by <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math>, with parameters <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta\in\Theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>θ</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi mathvariant="normal">Θ</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta\in\Theta</annotation></semantics></math>.
Given an input <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\in\mathcal{X}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>∈</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\in\mathcal{X}</annotation></semantics></math>, a response <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}</annotation></semantics></math> is generated from the policy, written as</p>
<table id="S2.Ex1" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex1.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∼</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\sim\pi_{\theta}(\cdot\mid x).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p1.2" class="ltx_p">The policy factorizes as</p>
<table id="S2.Ex2" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\prod_{t=1}^{|y|}\pi_{\theta}\!\big(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t}\big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∏</mo><mrow><mi>t</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></munderover><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>t</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mrow><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>&lt;</mo><mi>t</mi></mrow></msub></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)=\prod_{t=1}^{|y|}\pi_{\theta}\!\big(y_{t}\mid x,y_{&lt;t}\big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.1" class="ltx_p">For each input <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math>, we use a fixed reference policy <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>ref</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\mathrm{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math> to generate a pairwise preference set</p>
<table id="S2.Ex3" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="S_{x}=\{y_{w}(x),\,y_{l}(x)\}\subset\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.337em">,</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mo>⊂</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">S_{x}=\{y_{w}(x),\,y_{l}(x)\}\subset\mathcal{Y}^{\ast},</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the preferred response and <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> the dispreferred response. We denote the training dataset by</p>
<table id="S2.Ex4" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}=\{(x,S_{x})\}_{i=1}^{N}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><mo>=</mo><msubsup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></msubsup></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}=\{(x,S_{x})\}_{i=1}^{N}.</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.3" class="ltx_p">Throughout, we assume <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>&gt;</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math> for all <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\in S_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\in S_{x}</annotation></semantics></math> so that <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p2.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math> is well-defined.</p>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.1" class="ltx_p">To investigate the alignment between SimPER and REINFORCE objectives, we start from the REINFORCE objective and define its length-normalized variant. We consider the REINFORCE objective for paired offline preference data with masked rewards <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p3.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>R</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R</annotation></semantics></math> in Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition1" title="Definition 1. ‣ Notation. ‣ B.2 Theoretical Advantages of SimPER ‣ B Theoretical Background ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 1</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Define the masked reward <math id="Thmdefinition1.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}\to\{-1,0,+1\}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0.278em" rspace="0.278em">:</mo><mrow><mrow><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒳</mi><mo lspace="0.222em" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><msup><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒴</mi><mo>∗</mo></msup></mrow><mo stretchy="false">→</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">{</mo><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><mo stretchy="false">}</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R:\mathcal{X}\times\mathcal{Y}^{\ast}\to\{-1,0,+1\}</annotation></semantics></math> by</span></p>
<table id="S2.E8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x,y)=\begin{cases}+1,&amp;y=y_{w}(x),\\
-1,&amp;y=y_{l}(x),\\
0,&amp;y\notin S_{x}.\end{cases}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>{</mo><mtable columnspacing="5pt" displaystyle="true" rowspacing="0pt"><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr><mtr><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mn>0</mn><mo>,</mo></mrow></mtd><mtd class="ltx_align_left" columnalign="left"><mrow><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow></mtd></mtr></mtable></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,y)=\begin{cases}+1,&amp;y=y_{w}(x),\\
-1,&amp;y=y_{l}(x),\\
0,&amp;y\notin S_{x}.\end{cases}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(8)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.1" class="ltx_p">Since <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x,y)=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,y)=0</annotation></semantics></math> for <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y\notin S_{x}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∉</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y\notin S_{x}</annotation></semantics></math>, the REINFORCE objective for a fixed input <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> is</p>
<table id="S2.E9" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{x}(\theta)=\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\,R(x,y)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo rspace="0.111em">=</mo><mrow><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{x}(\theta)=\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\,R(x,y).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(9)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.2" class="ltx_p">Taking the expectation over the dataset <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p4.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\mathcal{D}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\mathcal{D}</annotation></semantics></math> yields</p>
<table id="S2.E10" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E10.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\big[J_{x}(\theta)\big]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mi>J</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">[</mo><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.200em" minsize="1.200em">]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\big[J_{x}(\theta)\big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(10)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p5.1" class="ltx_p">Based on equation <a href="#S2.E10" title="In Notation. ‣ B.2 Theoretical Advantages of SimPER ‣ B Theoretical Background ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a>, we now define the length-normalized variant.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmdefinition2" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_definition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmdefinition2.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Definition 2</span></span><span id="Thmdefinition2.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(Length-normalized REINFORCE objective)<span id="Thmdefinition2.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmdefinition2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmdefinition2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">Motivated by GSPO’s sequence-level objective <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib39" title="" class="ltx_ref">Zheng et al., 2025</a>)</cite>—which clips entire responses to exclude overly off-policy samples and applies length normalization to curb variance and place sequence-level importance ratios on a common scale—we likewise adopt length normalization and define the following REINFORCE variant:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E11" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,R(x,y)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>LN</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta):=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,R(x,y)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(11)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p6.1" class="ltx_p">We can now state the following proposition showing that SimPER implicitly optimizes the length-normalized REINFORCE objective.</p>
</div>
<div id="Thmproposition1" class="ltx_theorem ltx_theorem_proposition">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_title_theorem"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_theorem"><span id="Thmproposition1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Proposition 1</span></span><span id="Thmproposition1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold"> </span>(SimPER aligns with length-normalized REINFORCE)<span id="Thmproposition1.4" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">.</span></h6>
<div id="Thmproposition1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="Thmproposition1.p1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="Thmproposition1.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_italic">The gradient of SimPER’s objective equals the gradient of the length-normalized REINFORCE objective as follows:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex5" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex5.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>SimPER</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>LN</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.1" class="ltx_proof">
<h6 class="ltx_title ltx_runin ltx_font_italic ltx_title_proof">Proof.</h6>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.1.1" class="ltx_text">We start from SimPER’s objective function:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx8" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex6"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>SimPER</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mi>SimPER</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathcal{L}_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\exp\!\Big(\tfrac{1}{|y_{w}|}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)\Big)-\exp\!\Big(\tfrac{1}{|y_{l}|}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\Big)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\exp\!\Big(\tfrac{1}{|y_{w}|}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)\Big)-\exp\!\Big(\tfrac{1}{|y_{l}|}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\Big)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(12)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.2.1" class="ltx_text">Let</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex7" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="f_{\theta}(y\mid x):=\exp\!\Big(\tfrac{1}{|y|}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\Big)." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>:=</mo><mrow><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="false"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">f_{\theta}(y\mid x):=\exp\!\Big(\tfrac{1}{|y|}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\Big).</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.3.1" class="ltx_text">Using this notation, SimPER’s objective can be written as:</span></p>
<table id="S2.Ex8" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.Ex8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[f_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)-f_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>SimPER</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[f_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)-f_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.4.1" class="ltx_text">Taking the derivative with respect to <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx9" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex9"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex9.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>SimPER</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex9.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}f_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)-\nabla_{\theta}f_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>−</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>f</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\nabla_{\theta}f_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)-\nabla_{\theta}f_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.Ex10"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex10.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\Big[\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)^{1/|y_{w}|}\,|y_{w}|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>=</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\Big[\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)^{1/|y_{w}|}\,|y_{w}|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}\mid x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\quad-\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)^{1/|y_{l}|}\,|y_{l}|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\Big]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo>−</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><msup><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0.167em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\qquad\qquad\qquad\quad-\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)^{1/|y_{l}|}\,|y_{l}|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}\mid x)\Big].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(13)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.5.1" class="ltx_text">Since <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x,y_{w})=+1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>+</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,y_{w})=+1</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p7.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="R(x,y_{l})=-1" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi>R</mi><mo>⁡</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">R(x,y_{l})=-1</annotation></semantics></math>, we can rewrite equation <a href="#S2.Ex9" title="In Proof. ‣ Notation. ‣ B.2 Theoretical Advantages of SimPER ‣ B Theoretical Background ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a> as:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E14" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,|y|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\,R(x,y)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>SimPER</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,|y|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\,R(x,y)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(14)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.1.1" class="ltx_text">On the other hand, recall the length-normalized REINFORCE objective from Definition <a href="#Thmdefinition2" title="Definition 2 (Length-normalized REINFORCE objective). ‣ Notation. ‣ B.2 Theoretical Advantages of SimPER ‣ B Theoretical Background ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">2</span></a>:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E15" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E15.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,R(x,y)\right]." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>LN</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><munder><mo lspace="0em" movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta)=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,R(x,y)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(15)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.2.1" class="ltx_text">Differentiating both sides of equation <a href="#S2.E15" title="In Proof. ‣ Notation. ‣ B.2 Theoretical Advantages of SimPER ‣ B Theoretical Background ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">15</span></a> with respect to <math id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\theta" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>θ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\theta</annotation></semantics></math> yields:</span></p>
<table id="S2.EGx10" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S2.Ex11"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex11.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>LN</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.Ex11.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\nabla_{\theta}\left(\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\right)\,R(x,y)\right]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><mrow><msub><mo lspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo>(</mo><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup></mrow><mo>)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\nabla_{\theta}\left(\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\right)\,R(x,y)\right]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S2.E16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S2.E16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,|y|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\,R(x,y)\right]." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo>=</mo><mrow><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo>[</mo><mrow><mstyle displaystyle="true"><munder><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>y</mi><mo>∈</mo><msub><mi>S</mi><mi>x</mi></msub></mrow></munder></mstyle><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mrow><mn>1</mn><mo>/</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msup><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow><mrow><mo>−</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow></msup><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0.167em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mi>log</mi><mo lspace="0.167em">⁡</mo><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>y</mi><mo fence="true" lspace="0em" rspace="0em">∣</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0.170em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi>R</mi><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><mi>y</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>]</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo lspace="0em">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=\mathbb{E}_{(x,S_{x})\sim\mathcal{D}}\!\left[\sum_{y\in S_{x}}\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)^{1/|y|}\,|y|^{-1}\,\nabla_{\theta}\log\pi_{\theta}(y\mid x)\,R(x,y)\right].</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(16)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.3.1" class="ltx_text">Since the right-hand sides of equation <a href="#S2.E14" title="In Proof. ‣ Notation. ‣ B.2 Theoretical Advantages of SimPER ‣ B Theoretical Background ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">14</span></a> and equation <a href="#S2.E16" title="In Proof. ‣ Notation. ‣ B.2 Theoretical Advantages of SimPER ‣ B Theoretical Background ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">16</span></a> are identical, the following equality holds:</span></p>
<table id="S2.E17" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S2.E17.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta)," display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><msub><mo>∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>SimPER</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo>=</mo><mrow><mrow><msub><mo rspace="0.167em">∇</mo><mi>θ</mi></msub><msub><mi>J</mi><mi>LN</mi></msub></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>θ</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo>,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{SimPER}}(\theta)=\nabla_{\theta}J_{\mathrm{LN}}(\theta),</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td>
<td rowspan="1" class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_eqno ltx_align_middle ltx_align_right"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_equation ltx_align_right">(17)</span></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S2.SS2.SSS0.Px1.p8.4.1" class="ltx_text">which completes the proof. ∎</span></p>
</div>
</div>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</section>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">C </span>Further Details on FPA</h2>

<section id="S3.SS1" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.1 </span>Exact Formulation of FPA</h3>

<div id="S3.SS1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.p1.1" class="ltx_p">This section provides the exact equations for applying FPA to DPO, RPO and SimPER using Equations <a href="#S2.E1" title="In Training Dynamics ‣ 2 Preliminaries ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">1</span></a>,<a href="#S3.E5" title="In 3 Future Policy Aware Preference Learning ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a>.</p>
</div>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">DPO (with FPA)</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px1.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx11" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex12"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{FPA-DPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>FPA-DPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{FPA-DPO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex12.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.812em;" width="0.812em"><mtext>sg</mtext></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>β</mi><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex13"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex13.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 62.50009pt-\,\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.812em;" width="0.812em"><mtext>sg</mtext></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>β</mi><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 62.50009pt-\,\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">RPO (with FPA)</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx12" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex14"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{FPA-RPO}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>FPA-RPO</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{FPA-RPO}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex14.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big]-\frac{\alpha}{|y_{w}|}\Big)\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.812em;" width="0.812em"><mtext>sg</mtext></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>β</mi><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><mo>−</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mi>α</mi><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em">)</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big]-\frac{\alpha}{|y_{w}|}\Big)\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex15"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex15.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 62.50009pt-\,\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.812em;" width="0.812em"><mtext>sg</mtext></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mi>β</mi><mpadded style="width:0.437em;" width="0.437em"><mi>σ</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo>−</mo><mi>β</mi><mi>log</mi><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mrow><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mrow><msub><mi>π</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 62.50009pt-\,\text{sg}\!\Big[\beta\,\sigma\!\Big(\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{l}|x)}-\beta\log\frac{\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)}{\pi_{\text{ref}}(y_{w}|x)}\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3" class="ltx_paragraph">
<h4 class="ltx_title ltx_title_paragraph">SimPER (with FPA)</h4>

<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<table id="S3.EGx13" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody id="S3.Ex16"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{FPA-SimPER}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">ℒ</mi><mtext>FPA-SimPER</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\mathcal{L}_{\text{FPA-SimPER}}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex16.m2" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[\text{sg}\!\Big[\frac{1}{|y_{w}|}\exp\!\Big(\frac{1}{|y_{w}|}\log\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0em">=</mo><mo lspace="0em">−</mo><msub><mi>𝔼</mi><mrow><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><mi>x</mi><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo>,</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo>∼</mo><mi class="ltx_font_mathcaligraphic">𝒟</mi></mrow></msub><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mpadded style="width:0.812em;" width="0.812em"><mtext>sg</mtext></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=-\mathbb{E}_{(x,y_{w},y_{l})\sim\mathcal{D}}\Big[\text{sg}\!\Big[\frac{1}{|y_{w}|}\exp\!\Big(\frac{1}{|y_{w}|}\log\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{w}|x)</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
<tbody id="S3.Ex17"><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_eqn_cell"></td>
<td class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S3.Ex17.m1" class="ltx_math_unparsed" alttext="\displaystyle\hskip 62.50009pt-\,\text{sg}\!\Big[\frac{1}{|y_{l}|}\exp\!\Big(\frac{1}{|y_{l}|}\log\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo rspace="0.392em">−</mo><mpadded style="width:0.812em;" width="0.812em"><mtext>sg</mtext></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">[</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mpadded style="width:1.370em;" width="1.370em"><mi>exp</mi></mpadded><mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">(</mo><mstyle displaystyle="true"><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mrow><mo stretchy="false">|</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo stretchy="false">|</mo></mrow></mfrac></mstyle><mi>log</mi><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em" rspace="0.337em">]</mo></mrow><mi>log</mi><msub><mi>π</mi><mi>θ</mi></msub><mrow><mo stretchy="false">(</mo><msub><mi>y</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><mo fence="false" rspace="0.167em" stretchy="false">|</mo><mi>x</mi><mo stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo maxsize="1.600em" minsize="1.600em">]</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\hskip 62.50009pt-\,\text{sg}\!\Big[\frac{1}{|y_{l}|}\exp\!\Big(\frac{1}{|y_{l}|}\log\hat{\pi}_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big)\Big]\,\log\pi_{\theta}(y_{l}|x)\Big]</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
</div>
<div id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.1" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{sg}[\cdot]" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>sg</mtext><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo stretchy="false">[</mo><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">⋅</mo><mo stretchy="false">]</mo></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{sg}[\cdot]</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the stop-gradient operator, and <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\hat{\pi}_{\theta}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mover accent="true"><mi>π</mi><mo>^</mo></mover><mi>θ</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\hat{\pi}_{\theta}</annotation></semantics></math> denotes the estimated future policy. It is worth noting that FPA with <math id="S3.SS1.SSS0.Px3.p2.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=0</annotation></semantics></math> does not yield the same loss values themselves, but the same gradient and hence the same training dynamics and results.</p>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S3.SS2" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">C.2 </span>Computational Cost of FPA</h3>

<div id="S3.SS2.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S3.SS2.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We analyze the computational overhead of <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FPA</span> discussed in § <a href="#S3" title="3 Future Policy Aware Preference Learning ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">3</span></a>. For preference-learning algorithms that already rely on a reference model, such as DPO, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.2" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FPA</span> introduces virtually no additional cost: it requires no extra forward passes and only requires the marginal cost of logit extrapolation, which is negligible. For reference-free algorithms such as SimPER, <span id="S3.SS2.p1.1.3" class="ltx_text ltx_font_smallcaps">FPA</span> does require an additional forward pass through the reference model to compute <math id="S3.SS2.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="h_{\text{ref}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>h</mi><mtext>ref</mtext></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">h_{\text{ref}}</annotation></semantics></math>. However, in our pipeline, the dataset is generated with respect to the reference model from the outset, allowing us to cache the corresponding logits during data generation. As a result, the additional cost reduces to a memory overhead rather than extra compute.</p>
<div class="ltx_pagination ltx_role_newpage"></div>
</div>
</section>
</section>
<section id="S4a" class="ltx_section">
<h2 class="ltx_title ltx_title_section"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_section">D </span>Main Experiment Details from § <a href="#S4" title="4 Experiments ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4</span></a></h2>

<section id="S4.SS1a" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.1 </span>Dataset Construction</h3>

<div id="S4.SS1a.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS1a.p1.1" class="ltx_p">To generate a preference dataset, we sample <math id="S4.SS1a.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="K=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>K</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">K=8</annotation></semantics></math> times for every question in the training sets of MATH and GSM8K. We use regular expression (regex) matching to identify correct answers. Trajectories with correct answers are labeled as preferred while those with incorrect answers are labeled as dispreferred. Any questions where all generated answers are correct or all are incorrect are discarded. Temperature sampling (<math id="S4.SS1a.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>) is used for dataset generation with a constant seed of 42 and 5% of the data is held out for validation. All inferences are performed on a single node with four NVIDIA A100 80GB GPUs with vLLM <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al., 2023</a>)</cite>. Table <a href="#S4.T5" title="Table 5 ‣ D.1 Dataset Construction ‣ D Main Experiment Details from § ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">5</span></a> shows the number of preference pairs generated.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.T5" class="ltx_table">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_table">Table 5: </span>Preference Dataset Sizes.</figcaption>
<table id="S4.T5.2" class="ltx_tabular ltx_centering ltx_guessed_headers ltx_align_middle">
<thead class="ltx_thead">
<tr id="S4.T5.2.1" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_th_row ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.2.1.1.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">Model</span></th>
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.2.1.2.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">MATH</span></th>
<th id="S4.T5.2.1.3" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_th ltx_th_column ltx_border_tt"><span id="S4.T5.2.1.3.1" class="ltx_text ltx_font_bold">GSM8K</span></th></tr>
</thead>
<tbody class="ltx_tbody">
<tr id="S4.T5.2.2" class="ltx_tr">
<th id="S4.T5.2.2.1" class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_th ltx_th_row ltx_border_t">Qwen2.5-Math-7B</th>
<td id="S4.T5.2.2.2" class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_border_t">28,783</td>
