</section>
<section id="S4.SS4" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.4 </span>Evaluation Protocol</h3>

<div id="S4.SS4.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.1" class="ltx_p">We evaluate model performance on the basis of Pass@1 accuracy on the respective test sets. All inference is conducted using the vLLM library <cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib14" title="" class="ltx_ref">Kwon et al., 2023</a>)</cite> on a node with four NVIDIA A100 80GB GPUs. For each problem, we generate <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n=8" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>n</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>8</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n=8</annotation></semantics></math> independent solutions using temperature sampling (<math id="S4.SS4.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="T=0.7" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>T</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>0.7</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">T=0.7</annotation></semantics></math>). We report the average accuracy over all 8 tries as follows:</p>
<table id="S4.Ex25" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<tbody><tr class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex25.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{Pass@1}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{c_{i}}{n}" display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>Pass@1</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mfrac><mn>1</mn><mi>N</mi></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><munderover><mo movablelimits="false">∑</mo><mrow><mi>i</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>1</mn></mrow><mi>N</mi></munderover><mfrac><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><mi>n</mi></mfrac></mrow></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{Pass@1}=\frac{1}{N}\sum_{i=1}^{N}\frac{c_{i}}{n}</annotation></semantics></math></td>
<td class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></td></tr></tbody>
</table>
<p id="S4.SS4.p1.2" class="ltx_p">where <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="N" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>N</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">N</annotation></semantics></math> is the total number of problems, and <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="c_{i}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>c</mi><mi>i</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">c_{i}</annotation></semantics></math> is the number of correct solutions for problem <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="i" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>i</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">i</annotation></semantics></math>.
To report statistical significance, we compute the standard error of the mean. This is calculated as <math id="S4.SS4.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\text{SE}=\text{std}/\sqrt{N}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mtext>SE</mtext><mo>=</mo><mrow><mtext>std</mtext><mo>/</mo><msqrt><mi>N</mi></msqrt></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\text{SE}=\text{std}/\sqrt{N}</annotation></semantics></math>. All results are presented in the format Pass@1 ± SE.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS5" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.5 </span>Details on § <a href="#S4.SS3" title="4.3 Further Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">4.3</span></a> Total Gain/Loss</h3>

<div id="S4.SS5.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS5.p1.1" class="ltx_p">From the evaluation protocol, we can calculate the question-level accuracy (i.e. number of times a question is correct / 8). We then derive the question-level accuracy gain/loss by comparing performance. We calculate Total Gain by averaging all question-level accuracy gains, and the Total Loss by averaging all question-level accuracy losses.</p>
</div>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS6" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.6 </span>Effect of <math id="S4.SS6.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS6.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>C</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C</annotation></semantics></math></h3>

<div id="S4.SS6.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS6.p1.1" class="ltx_p">Figure <a href="#S4.F10" title="Figure 10 ‣ D.6 Effect of 𝜆 on 𝐶 ‣ D Main Experiment Details from § ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">10</span></a> illustrates the impact of varying <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> on <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> for SimPER. While the effect is marginal for <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> and excessively large <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda=10" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi>λ</mi><mo>=</mo><mn>10</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda=10</annotation></semantics></math> actually decreases <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{w}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>w</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{w}</annotation></semantics></math> by a fair margin. This may explain the weak learning behavior exhibited under high <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> in Figures <a href="#S4.F6" title="Figure 6 ‣ Model Degradation. ‣ 4.3 Further Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">6</span></a>, <a href="#S4.F8" title="Figure 8 ‣ Model Degradation. ‣ 4.3 Further Analysis ‣ 4 Experiments ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">8</span></a>. Additionally, we can observe that the regularization strength on <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="C_{l}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><msub><mi>C</mi><mi>l</mi></msub><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">C_{l}</annotation></semantics></math> scales accordingly with a larger <math id="S4.SS6.p1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math>.</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F10" class="ltx_figure"><object type="image/svg+xml" data="2509.19893v1/figure10.svg" id="S4.F10.g1" class="ltx_graphics ltx_centering ltx_img_landscape" style="aspect-ratio:439/145;" width="439" height="145"></object>
<figcaption class="ltx_caption ltx_centering"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 10: </span>Preferred and dispreferred coefficient sizes for varying <math id="S4.F10.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\lambda" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi>λ</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\lambda</annotation></semantics></math> on SimPER</figcaption>
</figure>
</section>
<section id="S4.SS7" class="ltx_subsection">
<h3 class="ltx_title ltx_title_subsection"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_subsection">D.7 </span>Prompts</h3>

<div id="S4.SS7.p1" class="ltx_para ltx_noindent">
<p id="S4.SS7.p1.1" class="ltx_p">For Qwen2.5-Math-7B and Llama3.2-3b-Instruct, we use the following prompt in Figure <a href="#S4.F11" title="Figure 11 ‣ D.7 Prompts ‣ D Main Experiment Details from § ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">11</span></a>. For DeepSeekMath-7B, we use few-shot prompting to generate trajectories. (see Figure <a href="#S4.F12" title="Figure 12 ‣ D.7 Prompts ‣ D Main Experiment Details from § ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">12</span></a> <a href="#S4.F13" title="Figure 13 ‣ D.7 Prompts ‣ D Main Experiment Details from § ‣ Future Policy Aware Preference Learning for Mathematical Reasoning" class="ltx_ref"><span class="ltx_text ltx_ref_tag">13</span></a>)</p>
</div>
<figure id="S4.F11" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel">
<div id="S4.F11.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:71.9pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-41.4pt,7.5pt) scale(0.82755221256436,0.82755221256436) ;">
</span></div>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 11: </span>Prompt used for Qwen2.5-Math-7B and Llama3.2-3B-Instruct</figcaption><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F11.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="120.19" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 120.19" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,120.19) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 114.28 C 0 117.55 2.64 120.19 5.91 120.19 L 544.09 120.19 C 547.36 120.19 550 117.55 550 114.28 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 114.28 C 1.97 116.46 3.73 118.22 5.91 118.22 L 544.09 118.22 C 546.27 118.22 548.03 116.46 548.03 114.28 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:6.69em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="92.63" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 92.63)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S4.F11.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="S4.F11.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F11.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Solve this math problem step by step. At the end, make sure to finish the calculation and state the answer exactly once in the following format:
The final answer is 
<br class="ltx_break">boxed{X},
where X is your final answer.

<br class="ltx_break">Q:{Question}

<br class="ltx_break">A:</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F12" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel">
<div id="S4.F12.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:276.7pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-41.4pt,28.8pt) scale(0.82755221256436,0.82755221256436) ;">
</span></div>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 12: </span>4-shot Prompt used for MATH in DeepSeekMath-7B<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib17" title="" class="ltx_ref">Lewkowycz et al., 2022</a>)</cite></figcaption><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F12.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="462.66" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 462.66" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,462.66) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 456.75 C 0 460.01 2.64 462.66 5.91 462.66 L 544.09 462.66 C 547.36 462.66 550 460.01 550 456.75 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 456.75 C 1.97 458.92 3.73 460.69 5.91 460.69 L 544.09 460.69 C 546.27 460.69 548.03 458.92 548.03 456.75 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:31.44em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="435.1" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 435.1)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S4.F12.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem: Find the domain of the expression <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{\sqrt{x-2}}{\sqrt{5-x}}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow></msqrt><msqrt style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></msqrt></mfrac><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{\sqrt{x-2}}{\sqrt{5-x}}</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">Solution: The expressions inside each square root must be non-negative. 
<br class="ltx_break">Therefore, <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x-2\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x-2\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\geq 2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\geq 2</annotation></semantics></math>, and <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5-x\geq 0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≥</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5-x\geq 0</annotation></semantics></math>, so <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x\leq 5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">≤</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x\leq 5</annotation></semantics></math>. 
<br class="ltx_break">Also, the denominator cannot be equal to zero, so <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5-x&gt;0" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&gt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">0</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5-x&gt;0</annotation></semantics></math>, which gives <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x&lt;5" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">&lt;</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x&lt;5</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Therefore, the domain of the expression is <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\boxed{[2,5)}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></menclose><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\boxed{[2,5)}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">Final Answer: The final answer is <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="[2,5)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">[</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">[2,5)</annotation></semantics></math>. I hope it is correct.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem: If <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\mathbf{A}=2" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\mathbf{A}=2</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det\mathbf{B}=12," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐁</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det\mathbf{B}=12,</annotation></semantics></math> then find <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B})." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀𝐁</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B}).</annotation></semantics></math>
Solution: We have that <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\det(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B})=(\det\mathbf{A})(\det\mathbf{B})=(2)(12)=\boxed{24}." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0em">det</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀𝐁</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐀</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.167em">det</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">𝐁</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn></menclose></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\det(\mathbf{A}\mathbf{B})=(\det\mathbf{A})(\det\mathbf{B})=(2)(12)=\boxed{24}.</annotation></semantics></math>
<br class="ltx_break">Final Answer: The final answer is <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="24" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">24</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">24</annotation></semantics></math>. I hope it is correct.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem: Terrell usually lifts two 20-pound weights 12 times. If he uses two 15-pound weights instead, how many times must Terrell lift them in order to lift the same total weight?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution: If Terrell lifts two 20-pound weights 12 times, he lifts a total of <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cdot 12\cdot 20=480" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">480</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cdot 12\cdot 20=480</annotation></semantics></math> pounds of weight. If he lifts two 15-pound weights instead for <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math> times, he will lift a total of <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2\cdot 15\cdot n=30n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">⋅</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2\cdot 15\cdot n=30n</annotation></semantics></math> pounds of weight. Equating this to 480 pounds, we can solve for <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m18" class="ltx_Math" alttext="n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">n</annotation></semantics></math>:</span></span>
<span id="S4.EGx18" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="S4.Ex26"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex26.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 30n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 30n</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex26.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=480" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">480</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=480</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="S4.Ex27"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex27.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle\Rightarrow\qquad n" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mspace style="width:2em;" width="2em"></mspace><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">n</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle\Rightarrow\qquad n</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex27.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=480/30=\boxed{16}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">480</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">/</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">30</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=480/30=\boxed{16}</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.2" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.2.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Answer: The final answer is <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m19" class="ltx_Math" alttext="16" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">16</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">16</annotation></semantics></math>. I hope it is correct.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem: If the system of equations</span></span>
<span id="S4.EGx19" class="ltx_equationgroup ltx_eqn_align ltx_eqn_table">

<span id="S4.Ex28"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex28.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 6x-4y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 6x-4y</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex28.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=a," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=a,</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
<span id="S4.Ex29"><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_right ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex29.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle 6y-9x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle 6y-9x</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_td ltx_align_left ltx_eqn_cell"><math id="S4.Ex29.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\displaystyle=b." display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mphantom></mphantom><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\displaystyle=b.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.3" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.3.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">has a solution <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m20" class="ltx_Math" alttext="(x,y)" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">(</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">)</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">(x,y)</annotation></semantics></math> where <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m21" class="ltx_Math" alttext="x" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">x</annotation></semantics></math> and <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m22" class="ltx_Math" alttext="y" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">y</annotation></semantics></math> are both nonzero, find <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m23" class="ltx_Math" alttext="\frac{a}{b}," display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">,</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">\frac{a}{b},</annotation></semantics></math> assuming <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m24" class="ltx_Math" alttext="b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">b</annotation></semantics></math> is nonzero.
<br class="ltx_break">Solution: If we multiply the first equation by <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m25" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{3}{2}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{3}{2}</annotation></semantics></math>, we obtain</span></span>
<span id="S4.Ex30" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex30.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6y-9x=-\frac{3}{2}a." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi></mrow></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6y-9x=-\frac{3}{2}a.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.4" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.4.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Since we also know that <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m26" class="ltx_Math" alttext="6y-9x=b" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">y</mi></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">x</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">6y-9x=b</annotation></semantics></math>, we have</span></span>
<span id="S4.Ex31" class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_table">

<span><span class="ltx_equation ltx_eqn_row ltx_align_baseline">
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padleft"></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_align_center"><math id="S4.Ex31.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{3}{2}a=b\Rightarrow\frac{a}{b}=\boxed{-\frac{2}{3}}." display="block" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mrow><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mfrac><mo lspace="0em" rspace="0em">​</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi></mrow></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000" stretchy="false">⇒</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">a</mi><mi style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">b</mi></mfrac><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mfrac></mrow></menclose></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0em" mathcolor="#000000">.</mo></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{3}{2}a=b\Rightarrow\frac{a}{b}=\boxed{-\frac{2}{3}}.</annotation></semantics></math></span>
<span class="ltx_eqn_cell ltx_eqn_center_padright"></span></span></span>
</span>
<span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.5" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F12.pic1.1.5.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Final Answer: The final answer is <math id="S4.F12.pic1.m27" class="ltx_Math" alttext="-\frac{2}{3}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mfrac style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mfrac></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">-\frac{2}{3}</annotation></semantics></math>. I hope it is correct.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem: {Problem}
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:</span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</figure>
<figure id="S4.F13" class="ltx_figure ltx_figure_panel">
<div id="S4.F13.2" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_figure_panel ltx_transformed_outer" style="width:397.5pt;height:558.5pt;vertical-align:-0.0pt;"><span class="ltx_transformed_inner" style="transform:translate(-41.4pt,58.2pt) scale(0.82755221256436,0.82755221256436) ;">
</span></div>
<br class="ltx_break ltx_break">
<figcaption class="ltx_caption"><span class="ltx_tag ltx_tag_figure">Figure 13: </span>8-shot Prompt used for GSM8K in DeepSeekMath-7B<cite class="ltx_cite ltx_citemacro_citep">(<a href="#bib.bib31" title="" class="ltx_ref">Wei et al., 2022</a>)</cite></figcaption><span class="ltx_inline-block"><svg id="S4.F13.pic1" class="ltx_picture" height="933.81" overflow="visible" version="1.1" viewBox="0 0 550 933.81" width="550"><g style="--ltx-stroke-color:#000000;--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" stroke="#000000" stroke-width="0.4pt" transform="translate(0,933.81) matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 0)"><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#000000;" fill="#000000" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 0 5.91 L 0 927.9 C 0 931.16 2.64 933.81 5.91 933.81 L 544.09 933.81 C 547.36 933.81 550 931.16 550 927.9 L 550 5.91 C 550 2.64 547.36 0 544.09 0 L 5.91 0 C 2.64 0 0 2.64 0 5.91 Z"></path></g><g style="--ltx-fill-color:#F2F2FF;" fill="#F2F2FF" fill-opacity="1.0"><path style="stroke:none" d="M 1.97 5.91 L 1.97 927.9 C 1.97 930.07 3.73 931.84 5.91 931.84 L 544.09 931.84 C 546.27 931.84 548.03 930.07 548.03 927.9 L 548.03 5.91 C 548.03 3.73 546.27 1.97 544.09 1.97 L 5.91 1.97 C 3.73 1.97 1.97 3.73 1.97 5.91 Z"></path></g><g fill-opacity="1.0" transform="matrix(1.0 0.0 0.0 1.0 21.65 13.78)"><foreignObject style="--ltx-fo-width:36.62em;--ltx-fo-height:65.5em;--ltx-fo-depth:0em;font-size:10pt;" height="906.26" overflow="visible" transform="matrix(1 0 0 -1 0 906.26)" width="506.72"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_container"><span class="ltx_foreignobject_content">
<span id="S4.F13.pic1.1" class="ltx_inline-block ltx_minipage ltx_align_bottom" style="width:36.62em;">
<span id="S4.F13.pic1.1.1" class="ltx_p"><span id="S4.F13.pic1.1.1.1" class="ltx_text" style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;">Problem: 
<br class="ltx_break">Shawn has five toys. For Christmas, he got two toys each from his mom and dad. How many toys does he have now? 
<br class="ltx_break">Solution: 
<br class="ltx_break">Shawn started with 5 toys. He received 2 toys from his mom and 2 toys from his dad, for a total of <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m1" class="ltx_Math" alttext="2+2=4" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">2+2=4</annotation></semantics></math> additional toys. Therefore, he now has <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m2" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5+4=\boxed{9}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5+4=\boxed{9}</annotation></semantics></math> toys. 
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:
<br class="ltx_break">If there are 3 cars in the parking lot and 2 more cars arrive, how many cars are in the parking lot?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break">There are originally 3 cars in the parking lot. When 2 more cars arrive, the total number of cars becomes <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m3" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3+2=\boxed{5}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3+2=\boxed{5}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:
<br class="ltx_break">Jason had 20 lollipops. He gave Denny some lollipops. Now Jason has 12 lollipops. How many lollipops did Jason give to Denny?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break">Jason started with 20 lollipops and ended with 12 lollipops. The number of lollipops he gave to Denny is <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m4" class="ltx_Math" alttext="20-12=\boxed{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">12</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">20-12=\boxed{8}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:
<br class="ltx_break">There were nine computers in the server room. Five more computers were installed each day, from Monday to Thursday. How many computers are now in the server room?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break">There were originally 9 computers. From Monday to Thursday is 4 days, and 5 computers were installed each day. The total number of computers installed is <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m5" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 4=20" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">4</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 4=20</annotation></semantics></math>. Therefore, the total number of computers is <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m6" class="ltx_Math" alttext="9+20=\boxed{29}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">9</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">20</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">29</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">9+20=\boxed{29}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:
<br class="ltx_break">Leah had 32 chocolates and her sister had 42. If they ate 35, how many pieces do they have left in total?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break">Leah had 32 chocolates and her sister had 42 chocolates. Together they had <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m7" class="ltx_Math" alttext="32+42=74" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">32</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">+</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">42</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">74</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">32+42=74</annotation></semantics></math> chocolates. After eating 35 chocolates, they have <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m8" class="ltx_Math" alttext="74-35=\boxed{39}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">74</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">35</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">39</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">74-35=\boxed{39}</annotation></semantics></math> chocolates left.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:
<br class="ltx_break">Michael had 58 golf balls. On Tuesday, he lost 23 golf balls. On Wednesday, he lost 2 more. How many golf balls did he have at the end of Wednesday?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break">Michael started with 58 golf balls. After losing 23 on Tuesday, he had <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m9" class="ltx_Math" alttext="58-23=35" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">58</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">23</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">35</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">58-23=35</annotation></semantics></math> golf balls. After losing 2 more on Wednesday, he had <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m10" class="ltx_Math" alttext="35-2=\boxed{33}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">35</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">2</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">33</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">35-2=\boxed{33}</annotation></semantics></math> golf balls.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:
<br class="ltx_break">There are 15 trees in the grove. Grove workers will plant trees in the grove today. After they are done, there will be 21 trees. How many trees did the grove workers plant today?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break">There are 15 trees originally. After planting, there are 21 trees total. The number of trees planted is <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m11" class="ltx_Math" alttext="21-15=\boxed{6}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">21</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">6</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">21-15=\boxed{6}</annotation></semantics></math>.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:
<br class="ltx_break">Olivia has <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m12" class="ltx_Math" alttext="23" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">23</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">23</annotation></semantics></math>. She bought five bagels for <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m13" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math> each. How much money does she have left?
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break">Olivia had <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m14" class="ltx_Math" alttext="23" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">23</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">23</annotation></semantics></math>. Each bagel costs <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m15" class="ltx_Math" alttext="3" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">3</annotation></semantics></math>, so 5 bagels cost <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m16" class="ltx_Math" alttext="5\times 3=15" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">5</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" lspace="0.222em" mathcolor="#000000" rspace="0.222em">×</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">3</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">5\times 3=15</annotation></semantics></math> dollars. The amount of money she has left is <math id="S4.F13.pic1.m17" class="ltx_Math" alttext="23-15=\boxed{8}" display="inline" intent=":literal"><semantics><mrow><mrow><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">23</mn><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">−</mo><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">15</mn></mrow><mo style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">=</mo><menclose notation="box"><mn style="--ltx-fg-color:#000000;" mathcolor="#000000">8</mn></menclose></mrow><annotation encoding="application/x-tex">23-15=\boxed{8}</annotation></semantics></math> dollars.
<br class="ltx_break">
<br class="ltx_break">Problem:{Problem}
<br class="ltx_break">Solution:
<br class="ltx_break"></span></span>
</span></span></span></foreignObject></g></g></svg></span>
</figure>
</section>
